um.theonyxpath.com/member/1771-is_a_becca","name":"Is_A_Becca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T04:29:46-07:00","id":93379,"title":"","content":"And also my version of the Qedeshah's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/93378-embrocation-b-s-conversion\">Embrocation</a>, please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1771-is_a_becca","name":"Is_A_Becca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T13:35:08-07:00","id":99481,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/99477-belial-s-brood-blood-and-smoke-homebrewed-and-houseruled-updates\">Belial's Brood Updates and Tweaks</a> with some tinkerings to the Doulosi and Therion. Merits ahoy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:03:32-07:00","id":99486,"title":"","content":"The recent update to the Khabit got me in Mekhet mode, so I decided to update the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1M632HpLw11DFl9rzUzArZPx5f6m3SLH9S7SmmdWK034/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Hollow Mekhet</a> as a Clan.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Proto-Mekhet</u><br /> In the nights before the Mekhet joined the all-night society, there was a time when they did not so closely resemble the Kindred Clans. These Proto-Mekhet could not embrace as the Kindred do. They could only be created through the posthumous embrace, and it left them empty. Soulless. Hollow. Since joining the other Kindred in the Danse Macabre, the Mekhet have grown past this limitation, and tonight there are no more hollow Shadows skulking around, running and hiding from their own reflections. But there are some who believe they could still be created, if a modern Mekhet performed the proper funerary rites.<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Hollows<br /> <b>Bane (The Hollow Curse):</b> Poto-Mekhet do not leave any residual impressions of their presence. They have no shadow, no echo, no reflection, no footprints, and are not picked up on recording equipment of any kind. Any character who spends time in one\u2019s presence can make a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll contested by the Hollow's Humanity to notice the absence once per scene.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes:</b> Intelligence or Wits<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> Proto-Mekhet count as Mekhet for the purposes of qualifying for prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <u>The Ka</u><br /> When a Proto-Mekhet is embraced, its soul, or Ka, leaves its body, or Ba. This creates a Rank 2\u009f\u009f ghost anchored to the vampire. This entity follows the normal rules for ghosts. Like all ephemeral entities, Ka use the simplified attributes of Power, Finesse and Resistance. A Ka\u2019s Power is equal to the highest of its anchor\u2019s Intelligence, Strength, or Presence, its Finesse is equal to the highest of its anchor\u2019s Wits, Dexterity, or Manipulation, and its Resistance is equal to the highest of its anchor\u2019s Resolve, Stamina, or Composure. A Ka\u2019s Virtue, Vice, and Integrity are those its anchor had in life.<br /> <br /> All Ka share the same ban. Any meal prepared specifically for a Ka and appropriately set becomes an Open Condition for it. If the person who prepared the meal then invites it, by name, to dine with them, it must immediately materialize at the table and cannot leave until it has eaten all of the food that was prepared for it. Doing so fully replenishes the Ka\u2019s essence pool. Additionally, a Ka shares all of its anchor\u2019s banes except for sunlight and The Hollow Curse. For banes that refer to Humanity, use the Ka\u2019s Integrity instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations:</b><br /> All Ka have the Twilight Form, Image, and Materialize Manifestations. When using the Image Manifestation, a Ka can only appear in reflections, recordings, or other visual mediums, and has the same appearance as its anchor\u2019s image or reflection would. When Materialized, a Ka appears as a living shadow, disturbingly similar to a Strix, but in the exact size and shape of the shadow its anchor would cast, unless it uses the Mortal Mask Numen, in which case its appearance is identical to that of its anchor.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b><br /> All Ka have the Numina Dement, Mortal Mask, and Sign. In addition, they have two unique Numina: Snatch.<br /> <br /> <b>Consume Flesh:</b><br /> The Ka must be materialized to use this Numen. This Numen allows the Ka to regain Essence by consuming dead flesh. Each size category worth of flesh is worth three Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Snatch:</b><br /> The Ka must be using the Image manifestation to activate this Numen. It spends three Essence and rolls Power + Finesse \u2013 the target\u2019s Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance. On a successful roll, it reaches out from the mirror, picture, or screen, and pulls the target into Twilight. The target is then forced to manifest in the same medium as the Ka, and is trapped in that image for a number of hours equal to the Ka\u2019s successes. If the victim is killed while in twilight, the remains disappear. Otherwise, the victim is returned to the material world in the same spot he was snatched from when the duration ends.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-27-2014, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:41:28-07:00","id":99661,"title":"","content":"I would humbly like to submit the Markosian bloodline to this Homebrew Hub <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/99655-bloodline-markosian\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...line-markosian</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:24:22-07:00","id":99686,"title":"","content":"Can I just say how much I love that this resource exists? This community is awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:44:00-07:00","id":99702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=99486#post99486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The recent update to the Khabit got me in Mekhet mode, so I decided to update the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1M632HpLw11DFl9rzUzArZPx5f6m3SLH9S7SmmdWK034/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Hollow Mekhet</a> as a Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome, though the wording on the weakness is sort of vague. Every five minutes per dot of Humanity? Wouldn't that mean it's <i>easier </i>to notice I'm not human when I have high Humanity? Maybe it should be 7 - Humanity? Or a number of rolls at an interval of five minutes equal to your Humanity's social penalty? Etc.<br /> <br /> Also, what Influence does the Ka have? Where/What Condition can it make Image or Materialize around? Is the Hollow the Condition? Can it Influence the Hollow to make them Open so it can Manifest on its own, or can it only Manifest through its Ban?<br /> <br /> I like it otherwise. Nice work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-26-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T21:01:51-07:00","id":99712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=99702#post99702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is awesome, though the wording on the weakness is sort of vague. Every five minutes per dot of Humanity? Wouldn't that mean it's <i>easier </i>to notice I'm not human when I have high Humanity? Maybe it should be 7 - Humanity? Or a number of rolls at an interval of five minutes equal to your Humanity's social penalty? Etc.<br /> <br /> Also, what Influence does the Ka have? Where/What Condition can it make Image or Materialize around? Is the Hollow the Condition? Can it Influence the Hollow to make them Open so it can Manifest on its own, or can it only Manifest through its Ban?<br /> <br /> I like it otherwise. Nice work!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I had trouble figuring out how to word that. The intention is, if you're humanity 1 they get to roll to see if they notice your lack of shadow once every 5 minutes. If you're Humaniity 2 they get to roll once every 10 minutes. Humanity 3 they get to roll once every 15 minutes, etc. etc. up until Humanity 10 where they get to roll once every 50 minutes.<br /> <br /> The Ka follows all the normal rules for a ghost, so its influences should be its anchors (which would only include the vampire) and its influence effects should be Strengthen and Manipulate. It can materialize within [rank] yards of an Open Condition (which it creates by using Strengthen on its anchor, or due to its Ban) and it can manifest as an image in any visual medium (picture, film, reflective surface, etc.) within [rank x 3] yards of its anchor.<br /> <br /> Thanks, glad you liked it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-27-2014, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T21:03:53-07:00","id":99713,"title":"","content":"Perfect, that solves any issues I might have with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I applaud the thematic implications of the Ka sharing traits with Ghosts. Nice one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-27-2014, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T22:24:10-07:00","id":99764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=99713#post99713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect, that solves any issues I might have with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I applaud the thematic implications of the Ka sharing traits with Ghosts. Nice one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, although I can't really take credit for that. In the original writeup in Shadows in the Dark they're stated to function the same way as ghosts with a few exceptions listed. It's just that in the original there were almost more exceptions than there were actual traits in common, whereas I tried to bring them a bit more in line with the existing mechanics. I'm a little like the God-Machine in that I generally prefer to build on existing infrastructure than to create new mechanics from whole cloth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:56:20-07:00","id":99946,"title":"","content":"What if the Hollows use Humanity as a dice pool in a Contested roll against the Wits+Composure of the people thay interact with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:49:02-07:00","id":100164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=99946#post99946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Hollows use Humanity as a dice pool in a Contested roll against the Wits+Composure of the people thay interact with?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could also work. As always, I fully expect people to tweak my homebrew to suit their own games, so if you like some parts and not others I won't be the least bit offended if you keep what you like and change what you don't. That said, I do like your idea better, I always found counting the minutes of interaction to be too fiddly but wasn't sure how else to connect it to Humanity. Thanks for the suggestion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:07:05-07:00","id":101488,"title":"","content":"Could I get my Homebrewed version of the En bloodline added? Thanks!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/100959-feedback-on-homebrewed-en-bloodline\">Homebrewed En Bloodline</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:01:44-07:00","id":101703,"title":"","content":"@Hollow Mekhet<br /> <br /> How about instead of connecting Humanity to how noticeable the lack of shadow and so on are, making it influence how often or how severely your Ka effs with you?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Or possibly allowing vampires to reign them in to a certain degree, using Humanity as dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:31:51-07:00","id":101709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=101703#post101703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Hollow Mekhet<br /> <br /> How about instead of connecting Humanity to how noticeable the lack of shadow and so on are, making it influence how often or how severely your Ka effs with you?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Or possibly allowing vampires to reign them in to a certain degree, using Humanity as dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do like the idea of the Ka growing stronger as the Mekhet's Humanity drops, I wouldn't want to replace the risk of being noticed with it. The lack of shadow/reflection/echo/footprints/recorded image/etc is the actual Clan Bane, the Ka is just a quirk of the non-kindred Clan Template, at least in my vision.<br /> <br /> However, I've been trying to work out a way to increase the range at which the Ka can use its manifestations, because really, 6 feet away from the vampire being the maximum range for Image and 18 feet away being the maximum range for Materialize is pretty weak, but I didn't want to mess with the ghost mechanics too much, and I didn't want to increase the Ka's Rank because that would give it more Influences. Giving it an effective rank increase for the purposes of range from its anchor based on Humanity sounds awesome to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added to the google drive document &quot;for the purposes of Manifestation Conditions, treat the Ka's Rank as 10 - its anchor's Humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: I'm just avoiding making a double post, this is actually a new piece of material. Continuing with the theme of updating mechanics from the Clan books (and my ongoing Masquiem project), I humbly present <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hNssb3w0QxV6sTEs66qpd1uN49o3L7GS7Hh7zL2os58/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavia, Malkavians, and Dementation</a>. &lt;--- link to google drive<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Malkav\u2019s Disease</u><br /> <br /> Named after the first patient known to have contract it, Malkav\u2019s Disease, or Malkavia, is a contagious illness that afflicts Kindred and Kine alike. Malkav\u2019s Disease affects the mind of the patient, eroding their sense of reality and causing severe mental and emotional distress. Once each day, an infected character can make a reflexive Resolve + Stamina roll to resist its effects, as normal. The number of successful rolls required to beat Malkav\u2019s Disease is equal to the Blood Potency of the vampire it was contracted from (or, if it was contracted from a mortal, the Blood Potency of the vampire <i>he</i> contracted it from -2). Unlike ordinary diseases, Malkavia does not deal damage on a failed resistance roll. Instead, the character gains both the Afflicted and Delusional Conditions (the Storyteller decides the nature of your character\u2019s delusion). Once these Conditions are inflicted, the disease has run its course and the character need not continue making resistance rolls.<br /> <br /> Condition: Afflicted<br /> Any living creature or vampire who drinks your character\u2019s vitae contracts Malkav\u2019s Disease. If your character is a vampire, any living creature she feeds on contracts it as well. This Condition expires normally (without resolving) after a number of nights equal to the number of successes you were short of beating the disease. If your character is a vampire, it expires after the same number of months instead.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Malkav\u2019s Disease<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character empties every point of vitae from her system.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <u>Malkavians</u><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> The origins of Malkavia, and subsequently of those afflicted by it, is a matter of much contention among Kindred scientists and historians. The most commonly accepted theories are attributed to the Defiant scholar Nicholas Polaski, who performed some of the earliest medical studies on the disease. He coined the name \u201cMalkavia\u201d after his presumed Patient Zero, a Ventrue named Grigori Malkav. Polaski attributed Malkav\u2019s affliction to an evil agent in the patient\u2019s thoughts that he believed was be spread by a psychological process he called \u201cDementation\u201d. Modern medical science has disproved many of these ideas, but it was Polaski\u2019s findings that lead to the understanding of Malkavia as a disease rather than a curse. Tonight it is understood that the disease spreads through vitae, although infection through Dementation is still a commonly held misconception among the lay Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>The Becoming:</b> It is not well understood what causes certain patients\u2019 vitae to be permanently altered by Malkav\u2019s Disease while others recover in relatively short order. However, some Malkavia experts are beginning to theorize that the infected Vitae may act similarly to that of an Avus. In this model, Malkavia may not be a disease at all, but some form of infectious Bloodline.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Demented<br /> <br /> <b>Requirements:</b> Any Kindred infected with Malkav\u2019s Disease, regardless of Clan, can join the bloodline as though her sire was a Malkavian. Although it is always the player\u2019s choice whether or not her character joins the bloodline, the character herself need not desire, or even be aware of the change in her blood brought on by the disease.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Danse Macabre:</b> Among the ignorant, Malkavians are hated and feared as lunatics and plague-bearers. Many domains exile known Malkavians, and some even have them executed. Among the informed, the Demented present an opportunity for further study of their condition. Most ambitious Kindred scientists would consider unethical experimentation a small price to pay to get their names in the Ordo Dracul\u2019s medical books, right alongside Nicholas Polaski. As a result, only the most far-gone Malkavians are mad enough to reveal their nature. But, in a rare few domains, the hallucinations their madness causes them are regarded as nigh prophetic visions. In such courts, the Demented are often made trusted advisors to the Prince and respected above mundane Kindred, their affliction seen as a true gift.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Terminal Curse):</b> The Demented can never be cured of Malkav\u2019s Disease. She must continue to make resistance rolls each night no matter how many she succeeds at in a row. When a Malkavian fails a resistance roll and gains the Delusional Condition, the disease merely goes into remission until she resolves it. The Afflicted Condition does not expire normally for a Malkavian.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Disciplines:</b> A Malkavian retains the disciplines of her parent Clan.<br /> <br /> <u>Dementation</u><br /> <br /> The \u201cGift\u201d of those tainted by Malkav\u2019s infectious blood is Dementation \u2013 though most would be more inclined to call it a curse. The powers of Dementation are drawn from the madness brought on by Malkav\u2019s Disease, and a Malkavian can therefore only enjoy their benefits while suffering the Delusional Condition. Just as all vampires can sense their Kindred through the shared vitae of their sires, the Malkavians can sense their fellow Demented through a kind of shared delirium known as the Madness Network. All Malkavians with the Delusional Condition treat each other as sharing a twice-removed blood bond for the purposes of Blood Sympathy. Additionally, the Malkavians can draw twisted insight from their shared visions. When a character joins the bloodline, she gains the Omen Sensitivity Merit. However, she can only use this Merit when she has the Delusional Conditon. Finally, if another character is foolish enough to actually <i>listen</i> to a Malkavian\u2019s ravings, the Demented can pass her delusions on to anyone who lets her in. A Malkavian with the Delusional Condition can use Social Maneuvering to attempt to make her mark understand what she sees. If the attempt is successful, the Malkavian can resolve her Delusional Condition and give it to her mark instead.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-30-2014, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T02:38:14-07:00","id":101837,"title":"","content":"That's a very cool take on them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like it A LOT","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:17:39-07:00","id":104293,"title":"","content":"I liked it so much, that I got inspired by it to modify it further. It's still work in progress, however anyone is free to add comments in the google drive, so please, fire away suggestions of what can be tweaked, and what devotions could be added. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18yupJyjVeUKIuxhdeN8RbpEa7d59js_PvOBBWIMwt_k/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Malkav's Disease, v2</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:48:23-07:00","id":105142,"title":"","content":"Could my Mystery/Coil of the Undying be added to the list?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88189-homebrew-mystery-of-the-dying\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88189-homebrew-mystery-of-the-dying\"> Homebrew: Mystery of the Dying - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88189-homebrew-mystery-of-the-dying\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/88189-homebrew-mystery-of-the-dying </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This is, as far as I'm concerned, by first real stab at homebrewing rules and actually coming somewhat close to a finished product. It's a Coil playing on Humanity, </div> </div> </div><br /> many thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T12:20:47-07:00","id":115458,"title":"","content":"Here's my own take on the Alucinor: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rPxt855Ms1DGTmF8xl4IP1cNGfKDTRazIQNyLifoLkE/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...NyLifoLkE/edit</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T20:17:54-07:00","id":118229,"title":"","content":"Hey PenDragon,<br /> <br /> I know this took basically no effort, but I made a little change to your Gangrel-Norvegi bloodline to make them fit the Khaibit Devotion model for Bloodlines in B&amp;S.<br /> <br /> As a result of trying to fit everything in, they had some of their devotions folded into the discipline powers to make their Gift Devotions. The unfortunate thing is that this might make them pretty powerful for some people's tastes, perhaps too powerful. The beauty of it though is that you can really just cut out the second half of each of the Devotions and mitigate that for the most part.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think they should get shunted off into extra Devotions? Or what approach might be most suitable?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ahiv5iIaEKtaij3ECUGRyhXoXl1NZ24S-2-WHfZJSXE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gangrel Norvegi &amp; Bloodworking</a><br /> <br /> For anyone interested in using one of them, I imagine these guys as being less secretive than the Mekhet version of the Bloodline. Their abilities might attract the scrutiny of the Ordo Dracul, who see their means of feeding and control over Blood as a rather distinctive evolutionary branch. I imagine the Covenants still might shun them for their lack of fangs and their spooky powers, but they're pretty powerful allies. Given the new utility of Status and their powers not being secretive, I believe this is reason enough to ditch the limitation on what the Norvegi can purchase.<br /> <br /> I imagine their lack of fangs and close identification with the Bloodline's homeland makes for a close-knit network of members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-24-2014, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T01:48:06-07:00","id":118328,"title":"","content":"I think you forgot the links .. <img src=\"https://forum.th