on b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=121200#post121200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A suggestion that should resolve both issues: Make 'Dementation' a sub heading I can link to, that way anyone who clicks my link will head straight to the Devotions, but can scroll up to see other content.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be perfect! Thanks again, I really hate to be a pain about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:43:22-07:00","id":121225,"title":"","content":"Readded. Thanks for working that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:50:28-07:00","id":121238,"title":"","content":"Modifying these a little bit, looking for some feedback.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Forced March (Celerity 2, Resilience 2)</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene (One hour)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">This devotion serves as a popular means of overland transportation for Kindred who have learned to toughen their bodies to withstand the dizzying power of Celerity enough to aid their movement for hours on end. The vampire can reflexively spend Vitae to increase her running speed, multiplying her speed by [Celerity + 1] for one hour. While this version of Celerity is invoked, the Kindred cannot use any of Celerity's other active functions without disabling the Forced March, requiring it to be reactivated.<br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 1 Experience to Learn</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Vaulting (Vigor 2)</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene (One hour)</span></span><br /> <br /> This easily formulated Devotion allows the Kindred to spend 1 Vitae reflexively to multiply the amount of feet jumped by a Successful Strength + Athletics roll by her Vigor dots plus two. This allows the Vampire to jump even greater distances than the enhanced strength of Vigor typically allows. Obviously this power might be a Masquerade breach for anyone who witnesses the unnatural capability of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> <i>Diana is a Daeva who wants to make a vertical standing jump up on top of a semitruck, which is 12 feet tall. She rolls 4 successes on her Strength + Athletics + Vigor roll, allowing her to jump 4 feet up in the air. She spends 1 Vitae reflexively to activate Vaulting, which given her Vigor of 3, increases her jump height from 4 feet to 20 feet in the air. She deftly lands on top of the truck.</i><br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 1 Experience to Learn</i></span><br /> <br /> Changes made include lowering the Experience cost of Forced March to reflect that it's a minor trick that those Kindred who invest in Resilience and Celerity can rather easily figure out.<br /> <br /> Vaulting I thought might be more economic if it lasts for a scene. Really makes for some cool jumping Vampires. Do you guys think it should go back to being for one turn instead, or do you prefer it like this? I want to suggest it to one of the players in our group as a cool investment, worried the per turn cost might make it unattractive.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:54:51-07:00","id":121243,"title":"","content":"Forced March is good as is, in my opinion. <br /> As for Vaulting, in my opinion it either needs increased Vitae cost, or a lower duration, since just activating this, pretty much allows you to escape anything you want to escape from. And it comes from Vigor, the most aggressive of the physical powers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:09:53-07:00","id":121247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=121243#post121243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forced March is good as is, in my opinion.<br /> As for Vaulting, in my opinion it either needs increased Vitae cost, or a lower duration, since just activating this, pretty much allows you to escape anything you want to escape from. And it comes from Vigor, the most aggressive of the physical powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point. Which sounds better:<br /> <br /> 3 Vitae for a Scene?<br /> 1 Vitae for a turn?<br /> 1 Vitae for [Vigor] turns?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:13:54-07:00","id":121250,"title":"","content":"3 vitae for a scene or 1 vitae for [Vigor] turns sounds best. <br /> Pick one depending on your desires <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I'd probably go with 1 vitae for [Vigor] turns, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:17:02-07:00","id":121252,"title":"","content":"Vigor already improves jumping passively, multiplying successes by [Vigor dots + 1]. So a character with Vigor 3, who rolled 4 successes would jump 16 <b><u>meters</u></b> at no extra cost.<br /> <br /> Exceptional jumping ability is the oft overlooked advantage of Vigor.<br /> <br /> Edit: If meters is excessive, feet is a fine substitute. Movement is an abstract system after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 04-28-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:23:31-07:00","id":121257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=121252#post121252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigor already improves jumping passively, multiplying successes by [Vigor dots + 1]. So a character with Vigor 3, who rolled 4 successes would jump 16 <b><u>meters</u></b> at no extra cost.<br /> <br /> Exceptional jumping ability is the oft overlooked advantage of Vigor.<br /> <br /> Edit: If meters is excessive, feet is a fine substitute. Movement is an abstract system after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, it does? Ixnay Aultingvay, I guess.<br /> <br /> I can't believe I missed that. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T18:55:50-07:00","id":141972,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this exactly counts as homebrew so much as a glorified list, but I've had a few people request the link to the original thread I posted it in, and I've had good feedback on it. I've added some stuff as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Yossarian's Ad Hoc Requiem for Rome Conversion:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Senex</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Carthian Law (&quot;Corpus Juris&quot;)<br /> <b>Merits: </b>As with <b>Invictus </b>in <b>B&amp;S</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cult of Augurs</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Veneficia, but use the rules for Cruac in <b>Blood and Smoke</b>, albeit with Veneficia's dice pool<br /> <b>Merits:</b> As with <b>Circle of the Crone</b> in <b>B&amp;S</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lancea et Sanctum</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage:</b> Theban Sorcery<br /> <b>Merits: </b>As with <b>Lancea et Sanctum</b> in <b>B&amp;S</b>; optionally, it would make sense for them to also have a version of their advantage in the <b>Pit of the Nameless </b>scenario from <b>B&amp;S</b>, to reflect their tight knit community:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood and Smoke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Lancea et Sanctum members receive Retainer, Herd, and Haven dots equal to their Lancea et Sanctum Status. This reflects the church\u2019s collective pool of resources that they share amongst one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: If you took that option, it might be better to change out Retainer for Contacts. Give them more of that &quot;early Christians on the run from the Romans&quot; feel.<br /> <br /> <b>Legio Mortuum</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Blood Oaths<br /> <b>Merits: </b>For each dot of Status, Legio vampires gain a dot in <b>Professional Training (Soldier) </b><i>or </i>in a <b>Fighting Style</b>. Additionally, they may purchase the Invested Merit, but with Allies replacing Herd.<br /> <br /> <b>Peregrine Collegia</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage: </b>All <b>Carthian </b>and <b>Invictus </b>Merits, <i>except </i>Blood Oaths and Carthian Law.<br /> <br /> <b>Julii</b><br /> <br /> <b>Options:</b><br /> <br /> 1. Use the Ventrue Bane in <b>B&amp;S</b>.<br /> <br /> 2. Use the Julii Bane as written (it does fill the prerequisite of scaling with Humanity).<br /> <br /> 3. Use PenDragon's custom Daeva Bane:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Degenerate Curse</b><br /> Daeva are prone to whims, flights of fancy and acts of impulse. The further a Daeva\u2019s Humanity descends the more they find themselves compelled to act on their Dirge. A Daeva should act on this impulse at least [8-Humanity] times per chapter. This means a Humanity 7 Daeva is only slightly more degenerate than a normal vampire, while at lower Humanity they find themselves indulging at every opportunity. Daeva Draugr lose their mask entirely, and must act on their Dirge at every conceivable opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>4. Use this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clan Bane (The Debased Curse):</b> Julii are ruled by base desires. A Founder retains her mortal Vice: she cannot regain Willpower from it, but her Beast urges her to act on it all the same. Whenever an opportunity arises to act on this Vice, roll the vampire\u2019s Humanity. On failure, she gives in to the impulse and gains the Debauched Condition. While Debauched, she suffers a cumulative \u20131 penalty (up to \u20135) to further Humanity rolls to resist her Vice. Resolution comes when the Julii finally indulges herself, or has a meaningful connection with her Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-19-2014, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T20:13:05-07:00","id":142029,"title":"","content":"I love it! Another option for the Julii Bane might be the Decadent curse you and Thorbes came up with on the old forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T20:38:08-07:00","id":142044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=142029#post142029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it! Another option for the Julii Bane might be the Decadent curse you and Thorbes came up with on the old forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah! Lemme dig that up...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Decadent Curse:</b> Julii are prone to excess. It may be that the Embrace amplifies the desires and entitlement the noble-born Founders experienced as mortals, or, as some only whisper, it may be that the debauchery of the Striges has tainted them through the unholy covenant that led to their creation.<br /> <b>System:</b> Whenever a Julii wants to stop feeding, she must roll her Humanity not to become lost in the pleasure of the Kiss. On a failure, the Julii gains the <b>Indulgent Condition</b>:<br /> <b>Indulgent</b><br /> <br /> Your character wants to extend the pleasure of feeding as much as she can. She must drink at least double the Vitae she previously consumed before gaining this Condition, even if that would force her to exceed the limits of her blood pool. Excess Vitae are spent or vomited up (some monstrous vampires revel in this act).<br /> This is not Wassail. The character is in control of herself despite the compulsion, being able to change vessels from moment to moment if she so desires, just as long as she drinks at least 1 Vitae for roughly each turn until the Condition is resolved.<br /> Failure to do so (whether there is no more blood available or because she was forced to stop feeding by an outside force) may prompt an anger Frenzy check.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Julii clan bane.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Drink double the amount of Vitae as you did before gaining the Condition <i>or</i> enter Frenzy.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Suffer a Detachment roll due to the lengths you've gone to indulge yourself. </div> </div> </div>There were a couple of versions of that. I can't remember who came up with what...I THINK Thorbes was behind that revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T10:56:38-07:00","id":152692,"title":"","content":"Something that's occurred to me. The Toreador Bloodline of nWoD has Dominate as its extra discipline. The Toreador in cWoD had Auspex.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just me, but I imagine Auspex would be perfectly suited to allowing them to appreciate the emotional texture of individuals/artists/art and stuff like that. A certain sensorial obsession really makes sense for them. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> And as an additional thing, if the Toreador were re-done as a post B&amp;S Bloodline, would you guys give them Devotions, or a Gift? What kinds of Devotions/Gifts would you give them, if any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T15:27:33-07:00","id":153156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=152692#post152692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's occurred to me. The Toreador Bloodline of nWoD has Dominate as its extra discipline. The Toreador in cWoD had Auspex.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just me, but I imagine Auspex would be perfectly suited to allowing them to appreciate the emotional texture of individuals/artists/art and stuff like that. A certain sensorial obsession really makes sense for them. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> And as an additional thing, if the Toreador were re-done as a post B&amp;S Bloodline, would you guys give them Devotions, or a Gift? What kinds of Devotions/Gifts would you give them, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't think every bloodline needs to have a unique Gift or Devotions any more than every bloodline needed to have a unique Discipline pre-B&amp;S. I would just add Auspex to their Discipline list (I agree it makes more sense for the Toreador than Dominate), and add the additional weakness. If you wanted to give them a little something extra though, I would go with Devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T15:36:40-07:00","id":153181,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I honestly thought it might just be cool, but the biggest fix I think is appropriate is the Auspex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T03:32:14-07:00","id":153636,"title":"","content":"Their gift might be Free Acute Senses merit.. in my opinion Acute Senses is a lot more important to appreciate the art compared to Auspex...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T17:14:26-07:00","id":154307,"title":"","content":"So I made a minor updated version of the Toreador here, though I left the option to keep using Dominate in there, all it really serves to do is update their weakness to be GMC-like. I also made two Devotions that, while not necessarily exclusive to the Toreador, were most likely developed by the members of the Bloodline and can usually be found among them.<br /> <br /> I'd like some feedback on whether that version of their weakness is appropriate. Also definitely need some help on the Devotions. I know exactly what I want them to do, but I'm having a hard time figuring out how to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15bAD6D8xH5ODFHm5lico6-AvHUJgFHXBhr35XTmNJTo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Toreador</a> </b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking you can use their backstory as-is, roughly. Switch the word &quot;Dominate&quot; for &quot;Auspex&quot; in their write up and you're set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:42:11-07:00","id":154551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=154307#post154307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I made a minor updated version of the Toreador here, though I left the option to keep using Dominate in there, all it really serves to do is update their weakness to be GMC-like. I also made two Devotions that, while not necessarily exclusive to the Toreador, were most likely developed by the members of the Bloodline and can usually be found among them.<br /> <br /> I'd like some feedback on whether that version of their weakness is appropriate. Also definitely need some help on the Devotions. I know exactly what I want them to do, but I'm having a hard time figuring out how to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15bAD6D8xH5ODFHm5lico6-AvHUJgFHXBhr35XTmNJTo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Toreador</a> </b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking you can use their backstory as-is, roughly. Switch the word &quot;Dominate&quot; for &quot;Auspex&quot; in their write up and you're set.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the penalty to the roll should be - BP. Quality of the art gives little in this regard, since if the quality is bad than the Toreador will flame the art. If it's good he'll appreciate and perhaps even praise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T00:53:50-07:00","id":154612,"title":"","content":"You're right, fixed it.<br /> <br /> Also added an optional Bloodline Gift which is Acute Senses for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-31-2014, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:14:49-07:00","id":165397,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a Tokyo-centric bloodline for a character in a chat game I play on, figure I may as well post it here!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZF2I5rXRCCVdDoVMuUiCFnlzwiITX36YNpsgBkCvZ1c/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZF2I5rXRCCVdDoVMuUiCFnlzwiITX36YNpsgBkCvZ1c/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZF2I5rXRCCVdDoVMuUiCFnlzwiITX36YNpsgBkCvZ1c/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZF2I5rXRCCVdDoVMuUiCFnlzwiITX36YNpsgBkCvZ1c/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T01:48:50-07:00","id":170518,"title":"","content":"My Rotgrafen bloodline conversation:<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12YJjkYY7flhn1CuM1lL7Edkmm0SRkmDc_y3P3kWHYSE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Feel free to comment on the document. Main changes: Changed the weakness, added a Gift, added a new Devotion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apollinaire bloodline: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11tfRLfq_7GGjDcWTXcDZc8gEEO-gVUDbxT2gL_v3Y6A/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Main changes - Carrefour changed into 5 Devotions (for each power) using mostly Dominate and Obfuscate as prerequisites. Instead of Carrefour the fourth discipline is Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Iltani Bloodline: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Xtn0DN5Hvu6RO0gK9o76GRMRoun_xkzXuvPMci4ykpI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Main changes - Made the bane more harsh. Added a Gift to poison via bite (it only works on mortals, so it's not a problem, and this poison cannot be collected, thus even low level Merges to create poison is useful anyways..In any case comments appreciated, perhaps this is too much?)<br /> <br /> EDIT3: Childer of the Morrigan: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l7qPyPHf6v0zoIDtFE2Dt4DxXXP9XgfYN8VCLY6vVt0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>.<br /> Main changes: Rewrote the Depression derangement as a persistent condition. Also, made the optional inherent power ritual as the default gift. I think it's pretty balance, because someone using that ritual in combat would need two turns (one to activate the ritual, another one to touch the opponent) and two successful rolls (touching the opponent is after all, a penalized roll). In any case, this isn't much of a conversion, since it's pretty much only has content already produced, but I thought I'll share anyways.<br /> <br /> EDIT4: Lygos : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dS1iPKzW_SxetIUqXX6hX7Nc9LdzEHxe1s6rMHB-A0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Main Changes - Added a bloodline gift.<br /> <br /> EDIT5: Cockscomb Society: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16yCVMeBTNGr-Fh49z39vwo4e-5b0FPPPsF8po42c_Ww/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Main Changes: Added a gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 06-18-2014, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T05:38:06-07:00","id":175939,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yIjIxhuVMBL1qWNfGSYM03nP7vSICwa2H0H_0ZJYlwk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">B&amp;S Malocusian bloodline.</a> Posting this in a separate post (unlike the previous bloodlines). To point PenDragon back to those (since he didn't notice the edits) and to note and ask for comments on Malocusians, since they are my biggest changed bloodline, turning this into a merit based bloodline.<br /> Also need suggestions for the last merit bonuses 3-5.<br /> <br /> EDIT1. Spina: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Zf9ERI8DZVp3-A3GDDysFmPTvnYeeMY2_HPCDJdo_5w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/docum