"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:27:15-07:00","id":181804,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1771-is_a_becca\">Is_A_Becca</a> took my Malocusian bloodline and vastly improved it. Can you mark <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1771-is_a_becca\">Is_A_Becca</a> next to B&amp;S Malocusian Conversion as a co-author? Or perhaps full author? I'm not even sure how that one should be credited anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T19:24:26-07:00","id":191900,"title":"","content":"I modified my version of the Toreador Bloodline, dropping the Devotions because they weren't mechanically sound, and I didn't have much feedback on them. I've made the Bloodline Gift into the standard rather than optional, but included something to help set them apart: The Toreador can pick either Dominate or Auspex as their 4th in-clan dot. This is to reflect their dual nature as both connoisseurs and patrons. The connoisseurs can appreciate qualities of art and people that are invisible to the eye, while the patrons are capable of ensuring their artists remain loyal and productive.<br /> <br /> The way I figure it, it's just a quirk of the Blood. Some inherited his facility for Auspex, while others, were embraced with an inclination towards Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T11:14:48-07:00","id":192537,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15Y2-GdxUC7KQUd-PvNE_ziwcjAYXBiYGcD_3xvaHFT4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Duchagne Conversion</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:43:29-07:00","id":193387,"title":"","content":"My take on the Sangiovanni, minus rituals.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bwe_U8ZCU4OudhtOodunsg3KS3WAFom5uCvYnG1fgo8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bwe_U8ZCU4OudhtOodunsg3KS3WAFom5uCvYnG1fgo8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bwe_U8ZCU4OudhtOodunsg3KS3WAFom5uCvYnG1fgo8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bwe_U8ZCU4OudhtOodunsg3KS3WAFom5uCvYnG1fgo8/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:02:02-07:00","id":193397,"title":"","content":"You forgot to share that page with the internet. At the moment it just leads to &quot;request access&quot; page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T18:31:31-07:00","id":194174,"title":"","content":"Damn, thanks for catching that. I so suck at this modern age comp stuff...Hopefully I fixed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T18:36:48-07:00","id":194179,"title":"","content":"Looks good, though I'd love to see some mechanics for Cattiveria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T23:52:08-07:00","id":199726,"title":"","content":"I've taken a crack at updating the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1m-hgER_p0Riy250P3x4AyljYjVq1qBDq_mfcgBdObcQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">California Xiao</a> for Blood and Smoke, and I'd love some feedback. Kingjan really made more sense to me as a set of Devotions rather than a full-on discipline, so I'm trying to model them after the updated Khaibit; unfortunately I've only been able to come up with two devotions thus far, and I'd love some suggestions on making more. I decided to give them Nightmare because a lot of the powers that make up Kingjan are geared toward creating unnatural feelings of anxiety and disgust, and the &quot;Wave of Apathy&quot; power is actually quite similar in effect to the first dot of Nightmare in Blood and Smoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:47:12-07:00","id":200123,"title":"","content":"I love what you've done so far, but if I can offer a suggestion, I don't think they should lose the full benefit of the Kiss. I think they ought to gain an additional blood potency based benefit to manipulate the person they fed on instead, since Swooning is more than just a dice bonus. I think Mortify works well so far, but you could make a Condition for it. I don't have access to my bloodlines book right now, but I'll offer more suggestions when I get back to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T12:01:38-07:00","id":200320,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it! My intention with Oblivion's Kiss was that the Swooning condition would still apply, but with a modified benefit to the users social rolls. Of course, as written its' actually a penalty to users of the ability with a blood potency of 1... the Kerberos bloodline seems to have a similar problem with their &quot;The Hound of Hell&quot; gift. I was originally considering having Oblivion's Kiss simply grant a blood potency based bonus on Manipulation and Intimidate based rolls, to specifically compliment the Charmed condition and the first dot of Nightmare; do you think that would work better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T13:53:09-07:00","id":200368,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I wouldn't specify what attribute it applies to, rather that it just applies to &quot;manipulating people based upon your familiarity with their emotions.&quot; It cold apply to anything socially oriented, from Presence + Intimidation to Wits + Empathy, in my opinion. I do agree that's a problem for the Kerberos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:20:30-07:00","id":200439,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me; that's pretty much how the power works in the original discipline; I guess I've just been playing games like Pathfinder too much lately, where the policy is to use precise language in order to reduce the number of rulings the GM needs to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T17:48:51-07:00","id":201637,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm looking this over again to give a more detailed assessment, CatDoom.<br /> <br /> Man. You tightened it up nicely, and I really have no complaints about what you have so far. I like their Bane, I like their Gift, I really like your new version of Mortify as a Devotion, and think it works perfectly for a converted Kingjan.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna talk about Kingjan now and converting each of its levels of ability.<ul><li>So Degradation on its surface feels like a similar power to Mortify, but I'm thinking that there should be a subtle difference, namely that it should bolster the victim in the Xiao's presence while weakening them when they're away from it. <i>Before the Xiao can learn to drain his victims, he must perfect the practice of breaking them. When activating this power, the Xiao speaks calmly to the target, flattering her or otherwise expressing approval in an apparent attempt to bolster her confidence. In fact, the power is a subtle attack, designed to weaken the victim's ability to function without the Xiao. The vampire's words seem harmless enough, but the mystic undertone delivers a deeper, more insidious message: &quot;You are only at your best when you are with me.&quot; </i>So this is from Degradation. I'm thinking that you make the roll, and it also afflicts them with a Condition, where they either gain a dice-trick or a bonus in the presence of the Xiao, and they suffer that bonus as a penalty when outside of it. Maybe they gain a +2 to actions in the Xiao's presence and a -2 when they're outside of it. As a direct bonus to the Xiao, they maybe gain +2 or 9-again to either encourage the target to act or to stop them from acting, as the Xiao's approval and presence are the source of their confidence and ability. I think this makes sense as requiring Majesty as its prerequisite.</li> <li>You've converted Mortify, so it's all good. Great job on that.</li> <li>Similarly, you've converted Oblivion's Kiss, and it's excellent.</li> <li>Wave of Apathy is okay, I guess. It reminds me of Dread Presence in how it suspends Willpower usage, but unlike Dread Presence, it's all willpower usage instead of just offensive. I'd probably keep the effect, but give it some additional oomph. Maybe it just enhances Dread Presence by offering an alternate version which instead of granting a bonus to your character, makes it so the victims can't spend willpower at all and suffer a penalty to actions equal to Nightmare due to their apathy and fear of failure. That could work.</li> <li>Blessed Detachment sounds like some kind of inverse Blood Bond effect, but I'm not sure how to represent it mechanically. Hmm.</li> </ul>You've done a great job thus far, nice work!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T13:43:56-07:00","id":202347,"title":"","content":"Thanks a ton for the feedback and the suggestions. I think with your advice I'm ready to take a crack at another couple devotions soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: I posted a new version of Wave of Apathy; I worry that it might be too strong, since there are a lot of ways it could be used to really mess with a vampire. Then again, it can be resisted... so I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-20-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T21:38:46-07:00","id":202637,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not too keen on that.<br /> <br /> Some nitpicks:<br /> <br /> Maybe specify in that description of the cost that it's an Instant Action to activate? If I could suggest, maybe it costs no Vitae and works a bit like Cross-Contamination, in the sense that it's also a passive aura which can't be used while Awe or Dread Presence would be used. I think it should lower effective resistance by -1, then maybe dicepools which reflect proactive action suffer a penalty equal to Majesty or Nightmare. Maybe it lowers their Speed too, because they just can't push themselves hard enough. Stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T22:19:52-07:00","id":202660,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Cross-Contamination looks like a fairly good model to follow, though if I continue to stick with the formula set by the Khaibit bloodline I would need to make Wave of Apathy stronger, since it would be twice as expensive in terms of experiences. Plus, it shouldn't be too similar, since it would be pretty trivially easy for a Xiao to just buy Cross Contamination. I'm imagining it definitely still preventing the use of Willpower on active rolls, though maybe it could still be used defensively, and maybe lowering the victims' effective Resolve. Then again, something that makes the subject more vulnerable to Majesty doesn't seem to quite fit the theme, since the point is that you're sapping their passions, rather than making it easier for the vampire to kindle new passions in them. Then again, I suppose maybe you could reason that inflicting unnatural emotions on someone might be easier if they're &quot;emptied out&quot; first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:10:31-07:00","id":205424,"title":"","content":"Should I link my stuff in this thread instead of making a new one? I made a semi-serious catgirl Bloodline.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some people like it, some people think it's too silly. To those people I point out that the Players exist. (Also I plan on updating the Players and making them less pathetic)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T16:48:31-07:00","id":205438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205424#post205424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I link my stuff in this thread instead of making a new one? I made a semi-serious catgirl Bloodline.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some people like it, some people think it's too silly. To those people I point out that the Players exist. (Also I plan on updating the Players and making them less pathetic)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's bad, though I'm unsure why they're Kindred? They sound like something that would be more appropriate for maybe Changeling or Hunter? Not as a group, but as one of the monsters, especially since Mortal Remains did make a point of how not all monsters are absolutely evil and must be killed, but are still potentially dangerous.<br /> <br /> I think the advice on common Banes is a nice touch, but I'd probably include it under a separate header from their Bloodline Bane, which while including some aesthetics, doesn't seem to describe any mechanics to accompany them?<br /> <br /> Similarly, I understand from their second devotion that they can control &quot;foxfire&quot; but the devotion doesn't really seem to suggest what they <i>do </i>with it. Beyond give people Spooked once and light up an area (Mind, the Kindred don't suffer penalties to sight unless they're in total darkness, and even those are halved.)<br /> <br /> Their last devotion feels like it has a clunky description and mechanics. I think it could benefit from some simplification and streamlining. Maybe look to the Burakumin, the Sangiovanni and the like for some ideas of how to make it less complicated?<br /> <br /> You mention that they're so damn useful, but I don't really follow on why? They're hardly the only Bloodline that can talk to the dead, with others actually being better suited, between the Dragolescu and the Apollinaire. While all bloodlines are rare and that should be minded, it feels that their usefulness is overstated and that their role in the Danse Macabre isn't adequately explored.<br /> <br /> While we're mentioning other Bloodlines who have spooky ghost powers or spooky dead powers, what's these guys' raison d'etre? The Apollinaire are Bokors and have their relationship with Ghede, plus a great power for actually capturing ghosts in govi jars to support their bloodline. The Dragolescu learn to attract and devour ghosts to empower the Kindred Condition. The Sangiovanni raise corpses in service of the advancement of an interconnected and squicky family. I'm not really getting what the Nekomata <i>do </i>from this writeup.<br /> <br /> In your &quot;In the Danse Macabre&quot; section, you identify them as a clan, which you may want to amend to Bloodline, FYI.<br /> <br /> I also don't really follow on why they get Protean.<br /> <br /> The write-up feels like it's got a bunch of disparate elements which don't really work together. I think one thing I've found helpful is to try to figure out a unifying theme for what the Bloodline is or does, and build around that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:03:49-07:00","id":205445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205424#post205424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I link my stuff in this thread instead of making a new one? I made a semi-serious catgirl Bloodline.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some people like it, some people think it's too silly. To those people I point out that the Players exist. (Also I plan on updating the Players and making them less pathetic)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, really well done on the graphical presentation! I know nothing about graphic design so I don't know if it was a lot of work to make it look like it's right out of B&amp;S or not, but damn if it doesn't look beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:07:37-07:00","id":205448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205445#post205445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, really well done on the graphical presentation! I know nothing about graphic design so I don't know if it was a lot of work to make it look like it's right out of B&amp;S or not, but damn if it doesn't look beautiful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded on that. Nice job putting the art in there, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:26:27-07:00","id":205456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205445#post205445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, really well done on the graphical presentation! I know nothing about graphic design so I don't know if it was a lot of work to make it look like it's right out of B&amp;S or not, but damn if it doesn't look beautiful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too difficult, just a lot of little things. I pulled the Strix banner out of the book, but that comes in a block format. So I took a screenshot of the section, pulled it into GIMP, then cut out the shape and made sure to cut the same shape out of the Strix banner, like a cookie cutter. I made sure to keep the dropshadow and frayed edges, and then I went and <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/mu91t\" target=\"_blank\">made several banners</a> for my projects. Tweaking the actual lettering is just a bunch of fonts I got from Mr Gone's site with the same grey gradient that the things have in B&amp;S. I'm actually kind of proud of my headers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205438#post205438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of stuff that would be cluttery if I quoted all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually some of the best feedback I've gotten on them. I made them Kindred because originally they were a bit of a joke (catgirl gangrels). Eventually I expanded on that, made them Mekhet (the other clan in the running was Nosferatu). I could definitely do with a bit of expansion. And I'll admit I'm not actually familiar with most of the Bloodlines you named. Much as I love the way Bloodlines work, there are just a crapton of them. <br /> Essentially they're useful simply because they can talk to the dead. They're spymasters, and partly inspired by an idea for a character I had that no ST would ever want to deal with: A vampire with Blood Tenebrous, Kindred Medium, Animalism, and a ton of Allies and Contacts that are ghosts, spirits, and animals. Just essentially a person sitting at the center of a network of unseen spies and servitors. I could do with tweaking them (maybe even giving them a full rewrite) with that concept in mind. The Kitsune-bi also... as you said doesn't really DO anything other than make spooky light. I should probably tweak that a bit as well, maybe make it draw in ghosts or something.<br /> <br /> And the last power is definitely in need of a rewrite. I was originally trying to save space, but that just makes the mechanics bad. I was mostly trying to crib from the Quicken Dead ceremony from Geist. Their &quot;theme&quot; as it goes is just sort of being these awkward, weird cat people who talk to ghosts and do weird unsettling cat things. But I feel like that might not entirely come through as it is now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't really follow on why they get Protean. </div> </div> </div>I felt it was wrong to give them weird features (there also are intentionally no mechanics for it; I was tempted to give them the Nosferatu drawback, but felt that having them be walking Masquerade violations was already bad enough) that they can push away with Protean but not give them Protean. It felt wrong to have an animalistic clan without it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:30:07-07:00","id":205458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205448#post205448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconded on that. Nice job putting the art in there, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should mention that it's not actually my art there. I think it might be Touhou fan art, but the creepy cuteness seemed to fit what I was going for. Especially the heterochromia.<br /> <br /> Fun fact, all heterochromatic cats have one blue eye. I've used the fluff before that cats with heterochromia see into Twilight with the blue eye. In reality it just gives them an increased chance of deafness due to the same gene causing potential degeneration of the cochlea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T18:06:48-07:00","id":205506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205424#post205424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I link my stuff in this thread instead of making a new one? I made a semi-serious catgirl Bloodline.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mediafire.com/view/484999d8v72u7sb/Nekomata.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some people like it, some people think it's too silly. To those people I point out that the Players exist. (Also I plan on updating the Players and making them less pathetic)</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like this concept, and you did a good job portraying them as serious. In addition to Leetsepeak's suggestions, I might suggest that, while Protean is definitely the go-to discipline for shapechanging, they might not necessarily need it, as it doesn't otherwise fit their concept. Perhaps go with Animalism instead, to let them do as you suggested and build up a massive information network of animal and ghost spies? Or if you wanted to drop one of the other Mekhet disciplines you could give them both. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of them being able to let a ghost possess a corpse and make a kind of ghoul/zombie servant. I feel you could differentiate it from the Burakumin and Sangiovanni corpse-raising abilities by emphasizing that the possessed corpse keeps the intelligence it had as a ghost; the previously mentioned bloodlines create mostly mindless servants, though they can potentially have a lot of them. Perhaps limit the number of possessed corpses the Nekomata can have at one time by their Blood Potency? <br /> <br /> I really like what you have so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T18:09:58-07:00","id":205509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205456#post205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually some of the best feedback I've gotten on them. I made them Kindred because originally they were a bit of a joke (catgirl gangrels). Eventually I expanded on that, made them Mekhet (the other clan in the running was Nosferatu). I could definitely do with a bit of expansion. And I'll admit I'm not actually familiar with most of the Bloodlines you named. Much as I love the way Bloodlines work, there are just a crapton of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. You can look most of them up here or there, they're all Bloodlines that deal with the dead and with ghosts, so it might be valuable to track them down and read up on them, because they give a good sense of different ways to go with it. For what it's worth, I think there's a lot going on here, and narrowing down what the essential elements of the bloodline are would be a good decision for picking one.<br /> <br /> For instance, I think the Protean bit doesn't really seem appropriate. Their curse and the unearthly nature of it sounds more appropriate for the Nosferatu, I think. As an additional reason, the Nosferatu Clanbook discusses how the Haunt's cthonic origins and associations give them a strong connection to ghosts and whatnot. It even includes a few merits to model that relationship. Essentially, there's a lot to work with there for a bloodline which is weird, unearthly looking and has a relationship with graveyards and ghosts. Since this element seems to be the most prevalent, there's a lot more to work with there than I think there is for a Mekhet or for a Gangrel, so my vote would be for them to be Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Now, there's another thing which is important to discuss, namely their mythological origin and that association. I think there's two things to address here: First whether the total mythology of the creature is appropriate for the Nekomata bloodline. I personally feel that it isn't, and that while they might share a name and associations, that they don't need to necessarily have cat ears or cat tails. These elements and the over-emphasis of their animalistic nature feel like extraneous elements which don't necessarily contribute to the theme. I can't make you do anything, but I'll say I don't think they need to be kept, or if they are, they should be revised to be more subtle and less overtly masquerade breaching. If you go along with their being Nosferatu, than I suggest things like their ears getting a bit unusual or maybe some kind of small, vestigial tailgrowth. Evoke the mythology a little bit, hew to the loneliness curse of the Nosferatu, and don't overdo the aesthetic and I think you'll get a stronger presentation.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm reading the wikipedia entry for the Nekomata, which talks about them eating people and bewildering/scaring them. So I think that's even more to work with insofar as their being Nosferatu is concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205456#post205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially they're useful simply because they can talk to the dead. They're spymasters, and partly inspired by an idea for a character I had that no ST would ever want to deal with: A vampire with Blood Tenebrous, Kindred Medium, Animalism, and a ton of Allies and Contacts that are ghosts, spirits, and animals. Just essentially a person sitting at the center of a network of unseen spies and servitors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is sort of the issue. Between the mythology and how it suggests more strongly for their being Nosferatu, it doesn't really feel like there's anything there for making them spy masters with ghosts. I'd actually go with another Bloodline for that, rather than try to insert it into the Nekomata write-up. Now, apparently in the mythology, they have a thing for siccing ghosts on people that wronged them. Not only does that sound pretty scary and sort of Nosferatu-like, it sounds fairly thematically unified with these other elements. They're Kindred who speak to ghosts. That's weird for the Kindred. Maybe, rather than the typical usage for ghosts being about spying on people, they use them against others to seek retribution or to aid them in hurting them?<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it, I think a concept for these guys COULD be a ghost spymaster, but that'd be more of an individual character's thing than the Bloodline's concept. Or at least, that makes more sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205456#post205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could do with tweaking them (maybe even giving them a full rewrite) with that concept in mind. The Kitsune-bi also... as you said doesn't really DO anything other than make spooky light. I should probably tweak that a bit as well, maybe make it draw in ghosts or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll stress that I think the ghost spymaster makes sense for an individual character concept rather than the bloodline's concept.<br /> <br /> For that Devotion, I'd make it something like burning Vitae (not literally, obviously) in order to attract ghosts. Maybe it marks the Nekomata as an Anchor for the nearest Ghost and draws them out. Maybe Ghosts can come to that location and gain Essence. The last one might be stepping on the Dragolescu's toes, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205456#post205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the last power is definitely in need of a rewrite. I was originally trying to save space, but that just makes the mechanics bad. I was mostly trying to crib from the Quicken Dead ceremony from Geist. Their &quot;theme&quot; as it goes is just sort of being these awkward, weird cat people who talk to ghosts and do weird unsettling cat things. But I feel like that might not entirely come through as it is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That concept once again sounds more Nosferatu than anything else. I'd suggest looking at the Burakumin or the Sangiovanni first, since they both have different takes on raising zombies, and would be a good place to start.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205456#post205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt it was wrong to give them weird features (there also are intentionally no mechanics for it; I was tempted to give them the Nosferatu drawback, but felt that having them be walking Masquerade violations was already bad enough) that they can push away with Protean but not give them Protean. It felt wrong to have an animalistic clan without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Protean really does much for their concept as it is. I think giving them Animalism as Nosferatu might be appropriate if they have powers over other cats and whatnot. Maybe as part of a Gift, or as a Devotion, they can use Animalism powers on Ghosts? That might actually be a more unique way for them to deal with Ghosts, since the Apollinaire already have the whole missing an eye, speak to/see ghosts thing going on, and it'd make them more unique. Maybe their Gift could focus around how Ghosts or things which seem to be like Ghosts interact with the different levels of Animalism.<br /> <br /> Still think some mechanics would be good for that Bane. Consider what you do with their Gift and their reason for being which can tie into it.<br /> <br /> I hope all that helps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:30:33-07:00","id":205585,"title":"","content":"Hrm. You're tipping me further and further towards the Nosferatu for them. I'd had this internal debate when I was first making them, and settled on Mekhet because I wanted to focus on this impression of &quot;they know all about you before you sit down because they've had someone watching you for weeks&quot;, but I'm starting to like the Nosferatu more, focusing less on the information and more on the spooky. And I might also get rid of Protean (and of course get rid of the bit where they can ignore their Bane by using Protean). I mostly settled on Mekhet because Auspex should ostensibly be necessary for the seeing into Twilight thing, but if I get rid of Protean I can always make their Disciplines Vigor, Nightmare, Obfuscate, Auspex. Of course, I've toyed with the idea of having them be from either Nosferatu or Mekhet. I like the idea of Bloodlines that allow members of different Clans. <br /> <br /> Time for a second draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:52:59-07:00","id":205613,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I get the association of seeing ghosts with knowing secrets/secrets beyond the grave and all that, but I really don't get that vibe from the Nekomata folklore, hence my suggestion to pursue the Animalism avenue.<br /> <br /> I also think that those Bloodlines which have involved multiple Clans (The Licinii, The Moroi? I think it's just those two) had that two-clan nature strongly integrated into their write-up, so if you were going that route, I'd suggest not doing it haphazardly, and putting a strong thematic emphasis on it. Personally, I don't think it's there if you want to do the Nekomata thing.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines which are just a change to the Kindred state are sorta different. These are the Sta-Au, the Therion and the Neglatu, and they're all written very specifically about it. Therion and Sta-Au are irreversible alterations to the Kindred state, and the Neglatu are pseudo-revenants, so unless that's integrated into the write-up and thematically jives, I don't think it's a good route to pursue. <br /> <br /> I'm speaking with an eye towards trying to keep the bloodline sleek, in the Blood &amp; Smoke style. It's good to keep it simple and not totally reinvent the wheel. Too many moving parts in a bloodline and you risk losing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:05:45-07:00","id":205628,"title":"","content":"Well, the idea was that since Nekomata can cause poltergeists and all that they'd talk to the spirits as well. As for the dual-Clan Bloodline thing, I actually was tempted to make them Mekhet/Nosferatu from the start. They'd have the Mekhet Bane for some catlike drawback (needing to drink bloody milk, being harmed by dogs barking, attracting cats, so on) but their hideous features would be from the Nosferatu Bane, and they'd be treated as having two less humanity when dealing with non-Touchstone muggles while their disfigurements weren't hidden away. I decided against that, and left the physical features without any real mechanics to them. <br /> <br /> That said, as you say, I have trouble with too many &quot;moving parts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T23:20:44-07:00","id":205769,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I think the dual clan bloodline thing's a good idea. As for devotions, you could build off of the ones in Khaibit's preview and work your way from there. An Auspex devotion could be used to see and contact ephemeral beings, while a Nightmare devotion could be used to intimidate or make them manifest. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 07-23-2014, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T23:57:49-07:00","id":205788,"title":"","content":"Is it weird that this bloodline reminds me of the Ahrimanes bloodline from Masquerade? I mean, association with cats, communication with spirits, Protean... I mean there are probably as many distinctions as there are similarities, but it just amuses me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T03:26:40-07:00","id":205871,"title":"","content":"A dual clan bloodline may work out better, IMO. While it's true that Licinii and Moroi are defined by their dual lineages, I don't know if the Nekomata fit perfectly as Nosferatu, considering that Vigor as a discipline doesn't seem to fit as well as Celerity does, and Auspex seems fairly important to them. Nightmare is good for scaring people, but doesn't do much else. Making them Mekhet that share the Nosferatu weakness could get their physical wierdness across, while keeping them with Disciplines that fit better for a ghost-seeing catgirl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T03:33:30-07:00","id":205877,"title":"","content":"But is htat really true? it just feels that you're tying them more to Mekhet than they deserve. Auspex doesn't seem important at all, in my eyes, speaking with ghosts and seeing other peoples emotions at a glance are totally two different things... as for Vigor, you could always exchange Vigor for Celerity and add animalism to the normal nosferatu roster <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T03:47:12-07:00","id":205900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205877#post205877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is htat really true? it just feels that you're tying them more to Mekhet than they deserve. Auspex doesn't seem important at all, in my eyes, speaking with ghosts and seeing other peoples emotions at a glance are totally two different things... as for Vigor, you could always exchange Vigor for Celerity and add animalism to the normal nosferatu roster <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's true, you could just give them a bloodline gift that lets them speak with ghosts, and devotions that work off of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T03:59:05-07:00","id":205919,"title":"","content":"Or a bloodline gift which allows you to See ghosts and apply animalism towards ghosts. That way, with first dot you get to speak with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:09:09-07:00","id":205922,"title":"","content":"At that point their clan doesn't really mean anything, though, if you just give them any old Discipline list. I see Auspex as being tied to the ghostly stuff because it's essentially seeing the unseen. Especially the Blood and Smoke version, where it's much less heightened senses and more knowing things you shouldn't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:23:01-07:00","id":205934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NjeUXNpm68xRdALApYkD6zAQddHWNKXAsxlm_cF7S5s/edit\" target=\"_blank\">My akhud</a> (everything is of my own writing except for Praestantia, which I borrow from PenDragon). Fluff still needs a bit of work. All comments are welcome.<br /> Note that they are quite different from other takes, that's mostly because they are tailored for my Hartford game. Hopefuly someone will find some use out of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At least as not as Loyal to each other version of them. Cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 07-23-2014, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:50:32-07:00","id":205949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205922#post205922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point their clan doesn't really mean anything, though, if you just give them any old Discipline list. I see Auspex as being tied to the ghostly stuff because it's essentially seeing the unseen. Especially the Blood and Smoke version, where it's much less heightened senses and more knowing things you shouldn't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was pretty much my reasoning for thinking they could keep Auspex. I do like the idea of a bloodline gift that lets them use Animalism on ghosts, though, and building the other devotions like foxfire and possessing corpses off of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:34:35-07:00","id":206218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JibKisamabi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=205949#post205949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was pretty much my reasoning for thinking they could keep Auspex. I do like the idea of a bloodline gift that lets them use Animalism on ghosts, though, and building the other devotions like foxfire and possessing corpses off of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'd push for Animalism. Giving them Auspex feels a little, I dunno... A little too expected, besides there isn't anything in the mythology to suggest he Nekomata know people's secrets.<br /> <br /> Having Animalism and having their Gift and Devotions be based around using it on ghosts would be unique and make the Bloodline stand out among those who can fiddle with ghosts. Additionally, it could explain the Nekomata's association with common housecats and the like, if they're using Animalism to see what they see and learn what they learn. Imagine, your cat is the only one around to witness your wrongdoing. The Nekomata learns of it through your cat, and sends Ghosts to harm you. When your cat shows up with ghosts in tow, it seems an awful lot like your cat just did something spooky. Enter the basis for the legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:45:55-07:00","id":206230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=206218#post206218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I'd push for Animalism. Giving them Auspex feels a little, I dunno... A little too expected, besides there isn't anything in the mythology to suggest he Nekomata know people's secrets.<br /> <br /> Having Animalism and having their Gift and Devotions be based around using it on ghosts would be unique and make the Bloodline stand out among those who can fiddle with ghosts. Additionally, it could explain the Nekomata's association with common housecats and the like, if they're using Animalism to see what they see and learn what they learn. Imagine, your cat is the only one around to witness your wrongdoing. The Nekomata learns of it through your cat, and sends Ghosts to harm you. When your cat shows up with ghosts in tow, it seems an awful lot like your cat just did something spooky. Enter the basis for the legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that going with Animalism fits, and I really like the idea of using Animalism on ghosts and building up an information network with it. I'm just not sure that they shouldn't also have Auspex <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The idea of a mysterious woman in a graveyard that seems to know yourself better than you do just appeals to me, I suppose. All of this is IMO of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:49:39-07:00","id":206235,"title":"","content":"The idea appeals, but is this the best fit for this bloodline? Your idea is fully realizable by mundane Mekhet clan if you ever want to play such a concept <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T10:39:59-07:00","id":206296,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's the same as the whole spymaster notion, I think it fits for a particular character, even a particular character within the Bloodline (Better find a Mekhet, or discuss with your ST the option of starting with Auspex [though it'd still be out-of-clan costs]) but trying to attach it to the <i>bloodline's </i>concept adds unnecessary chaff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T23:47:23-07:00","id":206792,"title":"","content":"Not to take up too much of the thread with my stuff, but I've also been kicking around the idea of updating the Players and making them less of a joke. I like them as they are, but they're very niche even as far as other Bloodlines go, and I don't really understand why any character would ever willingly join the Bloodline if they were at all aware of the All Night Society.<br /> I'm essentially making them a fusion of the Mekhet and Daeva clans. Obfuscate, Celerity, Auspex, Majesty. They have the Tenebrous and Wanton Curse. Their new fluff is that they're in on the joke, as opposed to deluded. I'm trying to focus on them as people who skirt the Masquerade, playing to the Vampire Lifestyle thing and getting groupies and blood dolls. They're playing at being Hollywood Vampires, as opposed to being just vampires who are obsessed with Hollywood, which takes up more of the write up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/jh6xlk2awo5a7s4/Players_B&amp;S.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">PDF</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T00:07:10-07:00","id":206798,"title":"","content":"Um, why exactly are they half Mekhet? (Besides the fact that it was so before) I don't suggest changing it, I just would like to learn what's so &quot;mekhety&quot; about them since all I see is Daeva..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T00:26:02-07:00","id":206800,"title":"","content":"Mostly because they were before. That's actually a good point that I'm surprised no one else brought up with me yet. Most people have complained that the mechanics aren't very interesting (and I haven't finished it yet, this is just a first draft without any benefits beyond the fourth Discipline, I plan on at the very least redoing &quot;Fakin' It&quot;) and that I completely miss the point of the Players. That said, I'd say that they reason they're Mekhet here is because they manipulative schemers (a &quot;Player&quot; after all is someone who's skilled at manipulating people by pretending to care about them). They're in many ways playing a big joke on Kindred society by taking on the appearances and attitudes of Hollywood vampires. And even influencing what the Kine consider a &quot;vampire&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T00:40:58-07:00","id":206821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=206800#post206800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>manipulative schemers</b></div> </div> </div> </div>um.. that sounds Daeva to me as well... Mekhets are the ones who know everything bout you. Daevas are the ones who'll manipulate you into doing exactly what they want you to, while being happy about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:21:57-07:00","id":207225,"title":"","content":"Mekhet scheme as well. For instance, there are a lot of references (that always seem like self aggrandizement to me) that there are no Mekhet Princes because they know not to attract bullets, and always manipulate the Prince instead of running the city themselves. They scheme, they collect information, they know everyone's business. Daeva make the Cacophony, and keep track of rivalries and who's doing what, but the Mekhet have their fingers right in the data stream.<br /> Hrm... that gives me an idea for another Bloodline...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T11:35:45-07:00","id":207351,"title":"","content":"Yes, but saying that they are &quot;Mekhet&quot; because of trait X, when the said trait X is also shared by &quot;Daeva&quot; is not the best of arguments, especially when we're looking for a reason why they are mekhet and not simply Daeva.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Cheers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T11:50:48-07:00","id":207371,"title":"","content":"Well, I <i>am</i> trying to make it a dual bloodline. It only makes sense that it would be focusing on a trait that's shared by both of the Clans","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:04:17-07:00","id":207385,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I totally agree with that, but I want to find a trait in Players which belongs to Mekhet so it's truly a dual bloodline, and not a Daeva bloodline with Mekhet thrown in, due to history.<br /> <br /> Do note, that I am not trying to argue, or seek change or anything. I just want to discuss this. (Since this might start looking like bickering)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:34:14-07:00","id":207410,"title":"","content":"Well, what would you suggest?<br /> I actually like the concept of a Social Mekhet Bloodline. Too much of them seems focused on getting information by listening in on conversations, or pouring over books. There's more than one way to get secrets, but they focus mainly on skulking and being <i>nerds</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T12:37:18-07:00","id":207416,"title":"","content":"Hm.. speaking of which.. perhaps the old Revelation, or whatever it was from Majesty? The one which forces you to spill all your secrets. Perhaps a Player devotion, Majesty + something? And suddenly, you'll telling all your juicy stories to this playah dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T23:55:39-07:00","id":207964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=207416#post207416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm.. speaking of which.. perhaps the old Revelation, or whatever it was from Majesty? The one which forces you to spill all your secrets. Perhaps a Player devotion, Majesty + something? And suddenly, you'll telling all your juicy stories to this playah dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually still covered by the new second dot of Majesty. Part of the Charmed Condition is &quot;revealing secrets that you really shouldn't&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:24:43-07:00","id":208092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=207964#post207964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually still covered by the new second dot of Majesty. Part of the Charmed Condition is &quot;revealing secrets that you really shouldn't&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps a more empowered version of it? Just for the players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:09:04-07:00","id":208162,"title":"","content":"How do you make &quot;tell all your secrets&quot;, but better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:31:12-07:00","id":208175,"title":"","content":"Auspex + Majesty devotion<br /> With this devotion, you feel exactly the perfect questions to ask to pull out everything he wouldn't like to say. With leading questions, you unravel everything there is about your target. After all, with current majesty, he doesn't just spill your secrets without encouragement, right? I don't know.. just pulling for straws here to find something mekhet-only to put in the Players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:07:16-07:00","id":209006,"title":"","content":"That actually does work.<br /> <br /> Also, I had a bit of an idea in the shower. <br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I want to focus on &quot;Mekhet + Daeva&quot;. So I'm going to make their main purpose manipulation of the Cacophony, and understanding it better than others. And I'll give them a new Bane. They take the original Bane of their Clan, then their new Bane is that people have trouble taking them seriously in direct discussion. They come off as silly or cartoonish in person, but when playing behind the scenes, they excel. Presence based actions will get penalized for low Humanity even towards Vampires.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Then again, that maybe feels like just a different kind of &quot;Majesty, but shitty&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I was thinking up a Devotion or Merit or whatever where they can manipulate the Cacophony through a Social Maneuver where they treat the Cacophony as having Doors equal to whatever the ST feel like (I might need to come up with a system for that) and then they treat the level and time between rolls as being based on their relevant Status. Through the maneuver, they can manipulate the Cacophony, making up rumours or quashing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T22:27:49-07:00","id":209048,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a whole lot of system for achieving something which seems part and parcel to the Cacophony to me. Like, you could do that with mundane rolls, no need for a supernatural power to do it. I could see why people would make fun of them in that situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T02:27:39-07:00","id":209220,"title":"","content":"I suppose...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:24:42-07:00","id":212672,"title":"","content":"So, I've been thinking about a couple of different mechanics for the &quot;Wave of Apathy&quot; devotion in my California Xiao re-design. In both cases the power would affect a single target, as in the original Kingjan discipline, and would require a contested roll between the Xiao and her victim:<br /> <br /> 1. The target loses a number of willpower points equal to the Xiao's successes, up the a maximum of her nightmare dots. At the end of the scene, the victim regains any willpower lost to this devotion (there is something of a precedent for &quot;refunding&quot; willpower points like this, in the form of the 4-dot ability of the <i>Riding the Wave</i> style merit.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2. All of the target's dice pools are capped by their Resolve+Composure for the remainder of the scene. This is farther from the original effect of the discipline, but seems thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> In either case this would be a proprietary Xiao devotion requiring Nightmare 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T13:35:59-07:00","id":213931,"title":"","content":"I kind of like #1 there, CatDoom. It feels distinctive but not too busy.<br /> <br /> At the same time, maybe make it so they lose Willpower equal to Nightmare automatically? At Nightmare 2, it's half the fighting reserve of a normal human, while at Nightmare 5, you're draining most people completely. The consistency of it might be a little mechanically cleaner and scarier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As an aside, you've made me realize that using Willpower on NPCs to <i>resist</i> PC actions is actually a good idea. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-30-2014, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:40:29-07:00","id":239318,"title":"","content":"Hey, any chance we could add my bloodline to the home-brew collection? <br /> <br /> found here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/231142-the-storytellers-bloodline-pishachas-from-india\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...has-from-india</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T05:22:02-07:00","id":258053,"title":"","content":"Last weekend I was in a Vampire event in Madrid. And Justin Achilli was there, given a chat abaout the game, and the diferent conflicts that move the game itself. He talked about Requiem too, and said that maybe, It should have been more diferent than The Mascarade. Thinking about that and reading all the stuff about the own-created Bloodlines I realized one thing Requiem should not have: Clans.<br /> The personal horror in Requiem has a main impact in Requiem, much more than in Mascarede, where many of the players turned their Vampires into somo kind of night superheroes. The word &quot;Vampire&quot; has in Requiem a much deeper feeling. Every city is diferent, there's no common origin for the Vampires, and in spite of the Covenents and the Coteries you are esentially alone. So I think the Clans should be suprimed. If I remake the game these days it would be without Clans. Every player could create his own Vampire, with same main weaknes (sun, fire, blood, Beast, sleep...) and maybe a particular weakness chosen froma a large listo of them. But you woulb be, in esence, a Vampire. Alone in the night, with no clear past and no clear future. You would need the Covenant to Survive and to give you no-life a sense anda a porpuse, buy you could create any kind of Vampire. The Clans wouln't determine your personality, your clothes or your thoughts. Because the vampirism is a course, not a ticket for a Social Club. Ande you are the same person than before, but now you are coursed ando you have to learn who to &quot;live&quot; with thay whitout loosing yourself and become a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3876-shockbringer","name":"Shockbringer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T06:11:48-07:00","id":258067,"title":"","content":"Well... I don't see how removing clans achieves any of that. If you define &quot;your&quot; vampire as a socialite, and take Majesty, you might as well go with Daeva as a clan, and spare yourself the whole overhead of &quot;Make your own clan&quot;. <br /> <br /> As well as there are rules for playing clanless games suggested already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think Damnation city or Danse Macabre have these... (Or maybe Chronicler's Guide?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:08:48-07:00","id":258152,"title":"","content":"Requiem Chronicler's Guide pg.35 deals with all of the above regarding playing a clanless game, including the importance of covenants and handling weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:35:58-07:00","id":258236,"title":"","content":"After several years of running I've essentially dropped both Clans and Covenants entirely from Requiem. I replaced Clans with Bloodlines (converting the original 5 into Bloodlines themselves), which IMO are more intimate and better suited for a Tier 1 - 2 setting. Covenants were loosened, no longer assuming that all characters are in one of five distinct global structures. The end result is a Kindred society that is disparate, no longer bound together by common clans or organizations, with different regions featuring very different societal structures. It also allows a storyteller to get creative with single Bloodline Covenants, cults, weird crossover groups, and all sorts of other strangeness outside the 'core' presentation of the setting.<br /> <br /> Highly recommended if you're looking for a more personalized take on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:54:58-07:00","id":258429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shockbringer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=258053#post258053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last weekend I was in a Vampire event in Madrid. And Justin Achilli was there, given a chat abaout the game, and the diferent conflicts that move the game itself. He talked about Requiem too, and said that maybe, It should have been more diferent than The Mascarade. Thinking about that and reading all the stuff about the own-created Bloodlines I realized one thing Requiem should not have: Clans.<br /> The personal horror in Requiem has a main impact in Requiem, much more than in Mascarede, where many of the players turned their Vampires into somo kind of night superheroes. The word &amp;quot;Vampire&amp;quot; has in Requiem a much deeper feeling. Every city is diferent, there's no common origin for the Vampires, and in spite of the Covenents and the Coteries you are esentially alone. So I think the Clans should be suprimed. If I remake the game these days it would be without Clans. Every player could create his own Vampire, with same main weaknes (sun, fire, blood, Beast, sleep...) and maybe a particular weakness chosen froma a large listo of them. But you woulb be, in esence, a Vampire. Alone in the night, with no clear past and no clear future. You would need the Covenant to Survive and to give you no-life a sense anda a porpuse, buy you could create any kind of Vampire. The Clans wouln't determine your personality, your clothes or your thoughts. Because the vampirism is a course, not a ticket for a Social Club. Ande you are the same person than before, but now you are coursed ando you have to learn who to &amp;quot;live&amp;quot; with thay whitout loosing yourself and become a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clans prescribing the character's personality, dress, social standing, etc. is a very Masquerade thing. In Requiem they do no such thing. They're also largely a misnomer, as evidence suggests not only multiple origins for vampires, but often multiple origins for individual Clans. From an in-game perspective, it is likely there is actually no such thing as Clan as the Kindred understand it, they are just incorrectly assuming that because all of these vampires have similar powers they must share a common ancestor. As such, Clanless games are actually rather appropriate, but by default Clan exists as the package that delivers affinity Disciplines and inherent weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T06:48:39-07:00","id":265408,"title":"","content":"So, I've created an optional add-on to my writeup of the Alucinor. Rather than the devotion-based way I framed Insomnium, I've created an alternative form of it as Blood Sorcery, as I've always felt that the themes of Oneiromancy lend themselves to actual magic, rather than a few innate tricks.<br /> <br /> Please add this, and let me know what you guys think: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lIm-iyVqT1tGo7_yPn1FHyHC16Tw27xq5m8PfSlhTyY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> As a note, I have ideas for a lot more Reveries, but would love some feedback on how things look right now before I tack more on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 09-25-2014, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T07:36:31-07:00","id":265459,"title":"","content":"Seems interesting, tho I don't understand the unnecessary cap of BP+2 to the discipline. <br /> Besides that, care to write up an optional part for those who use Themes? And how this interacts with them? Perhaps something in the vein of what PenDragon wrote up for other sorceries? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T07:43:46-07:00","id":265462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=265459#post265459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems interesting, tho I don't understand the unnecessary cap of BP+2 to the discipline.<br /> Besides that, care to write up an optional part for those who use Themes? And how this interacts with them? Perhaps something in the vein of what PenDragon wrote up for other sorceries? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to be a balance equivalent to how Humanity caps the other sorceries (one way or another). I couldn't think of a better trait for it, though I'm open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> As for themes, I was considering that, I may add that on a bit later, sure. I DID try to use Blood Sorcery to create most of the effects, though a few do bend the rules a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T07:48:59-07:00","id":265468,"title":"","content":"If I may, added spoiling and baddacelli bloodline conversions for B&amp;S.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T09:26:36-07:00","id":265521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=265462#post265462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's meant to be a balance equivalent to how Humanity caps the other sorceries (one way or another). I couldn't think of a better trait for it, though I'm open to suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the point in that. What this sorcery is capable of, is easily doable with the current sorceries. <br /> Basically, this 