ess/vampire-the-requiem/280140-bloodline-conversion-bruja#post280140 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Filhos Des Bruja Sons of Bruja A bar fight broke out in Southern Arizona. Someone spilled a drink, someone said something about someone else&rsquo;s mother. The </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:39:29-07:00","id":290371,"title":"","content":"Two new ones up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/290353-bloodline-the-urchins#post290353\">Bloodline - The Urchins</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/282111-bloodline-the-stitchers#post282111\">Bloodline - The Stitchers</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:43:58-08:00","id":322369,"title":"","content":"Has anyone considered riffing on the &quot;Jiang Shi as kindred clan&quot; idea from Blood &amp; Smoke and adapting another of the weird beings from Wicked Dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T23:41:33-08:00","id":323466,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/318476-bloodline-nan-meijing#post318476\">Bloodline: Nan-Meijing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T11:25:27-08:00","id":336174,"title":"","content":"Not sure if 1e stuff is wanted, here's some stuff that's mostly conversions from Masquerade. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/collections/2440368/Vampire-The-Requiem-fanworks-and-gameaids?page=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/collections/2440368/Vampire-The-Requiem-fanworks-and-gameaids?page=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/collections/2440368/Vampire-The-Requiem-fanworks-and-gameaids?page=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scribd.com/collections/2440368/Vampire-The-Requiem-fanworks-and-gameaids?page=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T19:00:02-08:00","id":340352,"title":"","content":"I tried my hand at making a Coil a while ago, and eventually arrived at a concept and mechanics for all levels of it that I like. It is still a bit bare-bones in terms of fluff and it lacks any scales, but I thought I'd share it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Coil Of The Ouroboros</b><br /> <br /> The Ouroboros is a snake that devours its own tail, perpetually enduring by growing at the same rate it eats itself. This Coil is founded much on the same principle - to make the Curse a self-sustaining state that draws infinitely nearer to perfection. Of course, there is no such thing as a truly self-sustaining machine. But the Coil of the Ouroboros uses the principle as a guiding post for the changes it enacts on a Kindred's undeath, allowing them to sustain the Curse and use its gifts with their force of will alone.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*</b> Animating Will</i><br /> The vampire can pay a Willpower point to rise from daysleep instead of Vitae.<br /> <br /> <i><b>**</b> Water To Wine</i><br /> The vampire's maximum stored Vitae is increased by his Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*** </b>Drain The Spirit</i><br /> When draining Vitae through biting, the vampire can drain an equal amount of Willpower points from the victim. Feeding restrictions based on Blood Potency still apply for Vitae, but not for Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i><b>****</b> Lasting Passion</i><br /> Each time the vampire uses Physical Intensity, he can pay one Willpower point per Vitae used to make its effects last for the rest of the scene. However, he can spend no more Willpower than his Resolve this way.<br /> <br /> <i><b>*****</b> Will To Power</i><br /> The vitae cost of every Discipline and Devotion is halved (round up), but is never lower than 1. The vampire can pay the Vitae costs of Disciplines with Willpower points if he so wishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-14-2014, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T23:04:38-08:00","id":366085,"title":"","content":"Wow, just found this thread. Time ta git mah readin' pants on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T02:26:21-08:00","id":370823,"title":"","content":"PenDragon, I like what you did with Quietus and i noticed that you seemed to be creating the Assamites as a bloodline for it. I was wondering if you had any lmore info about their history as, at the moment , they only seem to have a parent clan and weakness. And of course the discipline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4743-the_knosferatu","name":"The_Knosferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T18:27:27-08:00","id":371672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=258429#post258429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clans prescribing the character's personality, dress, social standing, etc. is a very Masquerade thing. In Requiem they do no such thing. They're also largely a misnomer, as evidence suggests not only multiple origins for vampires, but often multiple origins for individual Clans. From an in-game perspective, it is likely there is actually no such thing as Clan as the Kindred understand it, they are just incorrectly assuming that because all of these vampires have similar powers they must share a common ancestor. As such, Clanless games are actually rather appropriate, but by default Clan exists as the package that delivers affinity Disciplines and inherent weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saw this while looking for pendragons quietus.<br /> Blood and Smoke's assumption that all clan members of a given city are related puts clan back towards how it is traditionally used outside of Vampire.<br /> I like the 5 clans and I think Clan Dynamic brings something to game even with Covenants. But I could understand a clanless game.<br /> <br /> One variation I've been toying with is Clan means the vampire family plus retainers(ghouls).<br /> What standard Vampire calls Clan I call kith and your childe can be a differing kith than you.<br /> What causes this isn't quite known. But throw in the fact that Clan Bane doesn't kick in until Humanity 6 and things get interesting.<br /> Is it disposition of the childe? Whichever proprietary discipline they learn first? Or something else?<br /> Does an elder who breeds true do it by strength of blood ? Or is he more careful in his choice of potential childer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:09:48-08:00","id":372782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Knosferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=370823#post370823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PenDragon, I like what you did with Quietus and i noticed that you seemed to be creating the Assamites as a bloodline for it. I was wondering if you had any lmore info about their history as, at the moment , they only seem to have a parent clan and weakness. And of course the discipline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I've got ideas around an Assamite Clan they are a) currently not written anywhere and b) have a fair amount of Mummy crossover. For the majority of homebrew I pretty much leave out the setting bits, partially because I find the crunch more fun, and partially because 9 times out of 10 someone is just going to use the Discipline and homebrew their own bloodline history/fluff.<br /> <br /> Here's the short version of what I've got:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The original Assamites were fedayeen, first generation Hashshashin under Hassan-i Sabb\u0101h (who in this setting was a Mummy, ala Mummy: the Curse). They were his cultists, followers to the death, when Hassan fell into descent they trained, when he rose they fought. However, shortly after the Second Crusade Hassan vanished, falling into a long durance from which none could wake him. The fedayeen began to fray and disband. Elders, for fear that the group would collapse entirely, made a dubious decision. They courted with kindred and bargained for immortality, such that they could survive the wait for Hassan's next revival.<br /> <br /> But it didn't come. They experimented with death, delving into the Shuet in hopes to uncover the secret of Hassan's slumber. The principles of entropy they uncovered did nothing to aid in raising their founder, but provided the insight that birthed the bloodline's unique Discipline: Quietus. Over the generations the elders moved from waiting, to anticipating, to preempting, acting out Hassan's will as they presumed he might see fit. In the modern era they serve Hassan in name only, acting more as mercenaries than freedom fighters. Assamites are an expensive hire, but there is no cleaner, quieter killer in the kindred world.<br /> <br /> A final note: The Assamites pass around several myths concerning Hassan. One being that Hassan has arisen, but forsook the Assamites for their immortal crime. Another is that Hassan continues to drive the Assamites secretly, communicating only with select members. Elders in particular encourage this second interpretation, claiming to speak with Hassan in their torpor. <br /> <br /> Final final note: I also renamed them the Fedayeen. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:27:24-08:00","id":372794,"title":"","content":"I like what you have going. Will work out very well for the story i have in mind. Only issue is the mummy angle. I haven't read much into that one as, shortly after i acquired it 2nd ed was announced. so I'm slightly hesitant to look at the older material in case it changes substantially XD.<br /> Thanks for the reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4743-the_knosferatu","name":"The_Knosferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T07:38:29-08:00","id":376203,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/376185-ghilan-the-eaters-of-the-dead\">Ghilan, the Eaters of the Dead</a> -- Basically a light 'alterni-vamp' in the style of the Jiang Shi from B&amp;S, inspired by ghuls and by Pisha from VtM: Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM 