rum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:53:24-07:00","id":516589,"title":"","content":"I just made a new Discipline! Check it out!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X36J68qdN5rBLvfeK_6HZXCn0eLwl8vn1Fbn3e72ikI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Rift - The Discipline of Hell WIP</a><br /> <br /> (I will add the descriptions and fancy flavor text later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T18:29:22-07:00","id":517479,"title":"","content":"Look what I made! <br /> <br /> (Or well, posted. Because i've been using this for a while now.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y-b84-N-7M6WtPprSL1isPqHfmeqYqpU8xyV0g4au9Y/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Enfurecerse - The Discipline of Smoke</a><br /> <br /> I will add the Devotions later. There are <i>Many </i>Devotions okay. (Damn imaginative players! *Grumble grumble.) <br /> <br /> The story of the Discipline is that it belongs to a very city-happy Bloodline of Ventrue that have been fighting a battle with the Architects of The Monolith over the city of Boston for quite some time now. The Architects in Boston want a utopian, clean, beautiful city of spires and progress while the Potentates (As they are called) want a claustrophobic nightmare with a sky shrouded in smoke and a terrified populace who need to wear masks so they don't suffocate to death.<br /> <br /> Guess which of them are the most avid Strix hunters you will ever find short of the Khaibit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:57:30-07:00","id":519926,"title":"","content":"Enfurecerse is beyond awesome, if abit powerful. <br /> I think I'll use it for the lasombra (we play with the 13 clans from CWOD in B&amp;S) instead using nwod obtenebration as its presented for the khaibeit. <br /> In concept they aren't so diffrent and Enfurecerse suits the feel of the lasombra better IMO<br /> with your permission OFC","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6081-matanli","user":"matanli","date":". 05-19-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6081-matanli","name":"matanli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:59:43-07:00","id":519931,"title":"","content":"What a great coincidence! That is the Clan they were meant for!<br /> <br /> Of course you can use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:03:49-07:00","id":519933,"title":"","content":"Fulgaris and rift are also cool, they made me think of daimoinon and path of the levinbolt, again from CWOD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6081-matanli","name":"matanli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T23:27:21-07:00","id":520557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>matanli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=519933#post519933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fulgaris and rift are also cool, they made me think of daimoinon and path of the levinbolt, again from CWOD</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rift\" target=\"_blank\">Rift</a>, is actually a Discipline in CWoD, back from the time when the writers hadn't made the ridiculously racist and unbalanced Kindred of The East, this was what eastern vampires used.<br /> <br /> Fulguris is based on InFamous 1-2, while Enfuricerses is a bit inspired by Second Son.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am actually working on making a form of Daimoinon in NWoD, though mainly inspired by The Abyss from Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:53:27-07:00","id":531212,"title":"","content":"Wow, I can't believe it's been almost a year since I first posted my partial update of the California Xiao for Blood and Smoke. I never intended to abandon the project; I guess I just got distracted by other things.<br /> <br /> In any event, I've recently come back to the bloodline, and I've taken a crack at creating devotions corresponding to the one and five dot powers of the first edition Kingjan discipline (Degradation and Blessed Detachment). I've also considered modifying Oblivion's Kiss such that it allows the Xiao to learn a mortal's Vice in addition to its current effect, since it seems thematically appropriate and could provide a small but interesting lasting benefit to the vampire's social maneuvering attempts. I'm interested to know if others think that makes sense, or if it would add too much to the devotion.<br /> <br /> In the spirit of giving credit where credit is due, I should mention that my version of Degradation was inspired by Jacob's version of Kingjan, which he posted <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=42279#post42279\">here</a>. I really like the idea of using the Addicted condition, both because it seems to fit the flavor of the power and because the Deprived condition weakens Composure, which in turn makes the subject more vulnerable to the Xiao's other abilities.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll re-post the link to my writeup of the bloodline; the new devotion are listed as Fanlin (Degradation) and Nippan (Blessed Detachment); I'm eager to hear what people think, and I appreciate any criticism you can offer:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1m-hgER_p0Riy250P3x4AyljYjVq1qBDq_mfcgBdObcQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">California Xiao (Google Doc)</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-29-2015, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:14:18-07:00","id":552527,"title":"","content":"While I'm not exactly the biggest fan of this piece of work; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/405640-lost-clan-grettir\">Lost Clan: Grettir</a> by LostLight does deserve to be on this list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:35:03-07:00","id":563686,"title":"","content":"Alright, I was going over Mummy, and I thought a bloodline linking Mummy and Vampire might be interesting.<br /> <br /> So here it is, the Mekhet Bloodline Sefen-Haqr.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3cm93Z3JLS29fbGs/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3cm93Z3JLS29fbGs/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3cm93Z3JLS29fbGs/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3cm93Z3JLS29fbGs/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T22:08:26-07:00","id":563732,"title":"","content":"I like the idea. It makes a good deal of sense that some Mummies would see vampires as useful to their cults, and if they had a good reason to dislike or distrust vampires there's a good chance that they would forget about it as they rested in henet.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure it's a good idea for them to have originated in the Nameless Empire itself. As far as I can tell, Mummies didn't really have cults until they arose during the first Sothic Turn during the late Old Kingdom. Furthermore, having a group of vampires knowledgeable about Irem seems like it might kind of interfere with the core themes of Mummy. The Arisen themselves often have only vague recollections of the Empire, and recovering those memories is one of their major goals. Also, the city of Irem itself seems to have vanished more or less entirely; any vampires who were there more than likely shared in its mysterious fate.<br /> <br /> Also, Mummy powers tend to be extremely potent, and I'm not sure it's a good idea to give a vampire bloodline access to the full range of Affinities and Utterances available to the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-22-2015, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:17:19-07:00","id":563758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=563732#post563732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm not sure it's a good idea for them to have originated in the Nameless Empire itself. As far as I can tell, Mummies didn't really have cults until they arose during the first Sothic Turn during the late Old Kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that it was supposed to be in-character, legends of the founding, but I could have made that clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, having a group of vampires knowledgeable about Irem seems like it might kind of interfere with the core themes of Mummy. The Arisen themselves often have only vague recollections of the Empire, and recovering those memories is one of their major goals. Also, the city of Irem itself seems to have vanished more or less entirely; any vampires who were there more than likely shared in its mysterious fate. </div> </div> </div>Well, they are only as knowledgeable as what they can dig up or remember through the Fog. I don't know if I touched on that at all. I considered giving the mummy and vampire instinctive memory of each other (not real memory, but a sense of <i>&quot;hey, you look familiar</i><i>&quot;</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Mummy powers tend to be extremely potent, and I'm not sure it's a good idea to give a vampire bloodline access to the full range of Affinities and Utterances available to the Arisen. </div> </div> </div>You're probably right. Definitely gonna cut out the Utterance access, but I think the Affinities are <i>roughly</i> on par with Vampiric disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:30:23-07:00","id":586330,"title":"","content":"Just dropping by to see if I could get <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/571810-converting-favorite-bloodlines-to-2nd-edition?p=574669#post574669\">my Galloi conversion</a> added to the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T14:57:40-07:00","id":590521,"title":"","content":"I would also like to get my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585413-a-try-at-updating-a-bloodline-macellarius-to-vtr-second-edition\">Bloodline: Macellarius conversion</a> added if its still possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanks in advance!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/533-daniel-p","name":"Daniel P","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:47:44-07:00","id":726633,"title":"","content":"A 2E conversion and merging of the two versions of the Coil of Slumber. If anyone can further develop this idea (especially with regards to Scales), feel free to do so. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>\u200bMystery of Slumber</b></span><br /> Torpor is a dreaded experience that few Kindred can hope to stave off. Some Kindred who manage to remain active for decades find cause to seek out the deep slumber. Others are simply forced into it through starvation or physical conflict. In any case, Dragons who pursue the Mystery of the Sleeper recognize the need to mitigate some of the dangers associated with actually being in torpor.<br /> <br /> Scales of Slumber are psychological in nature. Some involve prolonged sleep deprivation, others call for extensive periods spent in torpor. Regardless of methodology, these experiments are directed towards the Dragon attaining a degree of control over the Sleep.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Coil of Slumber:</b><br /> <br /> <u>The Sleep of Early Years (o)</u> -- The Dragon first learns to focus his sleeping mind so the call of the Beast is lulled, and dreams are easier to shrug off. He may add half his dots in this Coil (rounded up) to his effective Humanity for the purpose of determining the length of torpor.<br /> <br /> <u>The Sleep of the Just (oo)</u> -- The Beast is never truly at rest, even in the slumber of Daysleep. It hungers for more, denying the Man the true comfort of sleep. Dragons who have mastered this level of the Coil have learned to quell the instincts of the Beast while they lay in repose. They may regain 1 point of Willpower from Daysleep just as mortals do from a good night's rest.<br /> <br /> <u>Denial of Morpheus (ooo)</u> -- At this tier of understanding, the Dragon has learned to fight for wakefulness even when gripped in torpor. The character acts as though all torpor were voluntary, so may roll to attempt to wake up once per torpor period. A character in voluntary torpor may roll twice per base period.<br /> <br /> <u>Defiance of Hypnos (oooo)</u> -- The Dragon who reaches this tier of the Coil has grown more . He may now add his Blood Potency to all Stamina + Resolve rolls made to stay awake. Furthermore, he gains an Exceptional Success at three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> <u>Master of Dreams (ooooo)</u> -- Having surpassed its pull on his soul, the Dragon can choose how and when he may awaken from torpor just as he chose when to fall into it. When voluntarily entering torpor, he may set a predetermined event to automatically rouse himself from sleep. He may call for his slumber to end when touched or shaken, in a number of months or years, or even after the weakening of the Blood to a specific Potency. During this time, the vampire is still subject to other stimuli and possible interruptions to his slumber.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Scales of Slumber:.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T17:04:26-08:00","id":782557,"title":"","content":"I have a bloodline-in-progress I would like to suggest as an addition here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781660-bloodline-lazarenes#post781660\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781660-bloodline-lazarenes#post781660\"> Bloodline: Lazarenes - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781660-bloodline-lazarenes#post781660\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781660-bloodline-lazarenes#post781660 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It may not look like it, but this bloodline is partly inspired by the Cappadocians/Harbingers of Death from the Classic World of Darkness. More information will be </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thank you in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum