bloodline-bak-ra\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805100-bloodline-bak-ra </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Another bloodline converted into 2E mechanics. Bak-Ra Parent Clan: Mekhet Nickname: Childer of the Sun, Servants of Ra Disciplines: Auspex, Celerity, Majesty, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-10-2016, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:44:07-08:00","id":812916,"title":"","content":"I'd love to get my <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B0KDN_qcgXvwQkpjaTRxOEpFQXM/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Julii writeup</a> added to the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-20-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T04:08:22-08:00","id":821531,"title":"","content":"Tatterdemalion King, I really like what you did with bringing the Brood into Blood and Smoke/2E. Is what you have linked on the Homebrew Hub your most recent, or are you still tweaking it? I can see by the dates on this topic in another thread I'm a bit late to the party, but something I wanted to mention regarding the Brood, Humanity, Touchstones, Pursuit, etc...<br /> <br /> I don't see a problem with the Brood dropping Humanity and Touchstones in the long run, replacing it with the Covey or a Resonant. I see the Pursuit as a sort of marathon to realize the ideal vampiric condition, and part of that is coming to a Blood Potency that no longer requires feeding on humans for sustenance. I see the Brood using things like Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Investments, and Devotions when they have to interact with humans (as these aren't penalized by Humanity). Thus, it would not be a problem in the long run in their goal of the Pursuit to shed Touchstones and Humanity. Even at Humanity 1 or 2 (with or without penalties through a Bane and/or Mark of the Beast), with a Blood Potency Therion 9 to 10, the effective Humanity for waking, Torpor, etc, is still 5-7. That's really all they need; if they absolutely must interact with humans, they do so as vampires using Disciplines, Investments, Devotions. All the social interaction they would require is arguably received from their own Covey and/or the vampires they may be hiding among.<br /> <br /> In a way, elder Brood may be best at keeping the First Tradition. Once they no longer feed from humans, thanks to the Pursuit they also no longer need to maintain any relations with them. Thus, the Masquerade is preserved. And related to Traditions...<br /> <br /> Something else I found interesting regarding the Therion is how their bane essentially makes it impossible to break the Third Tradition. In a roundabout way, leaving the Brood also enforces an aspect of the First Tradition; they can't reveal what they don't know. This leaves Diablerie. Maybe something could be tied in with your Merits and other rules that does something similar for Diablerie (not allowing them to do it or getting no benefits from it)? I'd need to reread the Covenant book to see what their take is on Diablerie, but I like the irony of a group of vampires that embrace their Beast being the ones most likely or able to follow the three Traditions. And maybe this is why the other Covenants don't like them; in paradoxical fashion, the vampires least human are the ones best at preserving the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:15:31-08:00","id":822854,"title":"","content":"Please add the following!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e7YshOL8exLJMweN0ydxWTrQMZKhKpz7JsKeDfTvdO8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Mechanical Bloodline Updates:</a> I've realized it's sort of redundant providing fluff that's already mostly been covered by existing sources; most bloodlines just need you to update the discipline list (sometimes), the bloodline bane, and the bloodline gift. So, this is a project wherein I go through a crapton of bloodlines and update them all mechanically, without adding any extraneous fluff (past a sentence or two to describe the bloodline gifts).<br /> This is a big project that I'll be updating over time, but for now it has all of the core and the Hidden completed. May take me a bit to start on other sources; in the future I might start doing it more 'randomly', just updating ones that I find random inspiration for here and there, without committing to doing the entirety of a book at once. But we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:15:24-08:00","id":823592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub?p=822854#post822854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please add the following!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e7YshOL8exLJMweN0ydxWTrQMZKhKpz7JsKeDfTvdO8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Mechanical Bloodline Updates:</a> I've realized it's sort of redundant providing fluff that's already mostly been covered by existing sources; most bloodlines just need you to update the discipline list (sometimes), the bloodline bane, and the bloodline gift. So, this is a project wherein I go through a crapton of bloodlines and update them all mechanically, without adding any extraneous fluff (past a sentence or two to describe the bloodline gifts).<br /> This is a big project that I'll be updating over time, but for now it has all of the core and the Hidden completed. May take me a bit to start on other sources; in the future I might start doing it more 'randomly', just updating ones that I find random inspiration for here and there, without committing to doing the entirety of a book at once. But we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added.<br /> <br /> Also added your Tremere conversion which is, IMO, quite good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d